.TH SDL_FingerID 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_FingerID \- A unique ID for a single finger on a touch device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_touch.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef Uint64 SDL_FingerID;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This ID is valid for the time the finger (stylus, etc) is touching and will be unique for all fingers currently in contact, so this ID tracks the lifetime of a single continuous touch\[char46] This value may represent an index, a pointer, or some other unique ID, depending on the platform\[char46]
.PP
The value 0 is an invalid ID\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

